  <p>
    This website (<strong>mboiman.github.io</strong>) is a personal CV site with an
    optional AI chat assistant. Personal data is processed only to the extent
    described below. There is <strong>no tracking, no advertising and no analytics
    cookies</strong>.
  </p>

  <h2>1. Controller</h2>
  <address>
    Michael Boiman<br />
    Zum Gottschalkhof 2<br />
    60594 Frankfurt am Main, Germany<br />
    Email: <a href="mailto:mboiman@gmail.com">mboiman@gmail.com</a>
  </address>

  <h2>2. Visiting the website (hosting)</h2>
  <p>
    The site is served as a static page via <strong>GitHub Pages</strong> (GitHub,
    Inc., 88 Colin P. Kelly Jr. Street, San Francisco, CA 94107, USA). When you visit,
    GitHub processes technically necessary access data (including IP address, date and
    time, the resource requested, amount of data transferred, browser type) in order
    to deliver the page and keep operation secure and stable. The legal basis is
    Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR (legitimate interest in secure, functional provision).
  </p>

  <h2>3. AI chat assistant</h2>
  <p>
    The site offers an optional chat assistant (the agent). It answers questions about
    Michael Boiman's professional profile and takes inquiries and meeting requests on
    his behalf. Use is voluntary, your input is only processed if you send a message
    yourself. The same agent is also reachable for other software agents at
    <em>mboiman.bks-lab.com</em>. This section applies accordingly to messages sent
    that way.
  </p>

  <h3>Answers and logs</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Generating answers:</strong> Your message is sent to the agent endpoint
      <em>mboiman.bks-lab.com</em>. The agent runs on a computer owned by Michael
      Boiman. The answer is generated by a language model from
      <strong>Anthropic</strong> ("Claude"). For this, Anthropic receives your message,
      the conversation so far and the page context (next item). Transport runs through
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong>, which processes technical connection data (including
      IP address) to protect the service against abuse and overload.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>What travels with a message:</strong> Alongside your input, technical
      details are transmitted: the path of the open page, the selected interface
      language, the section currently in view, that page's anchors, which controls the
      chat window can display (such as suggestion buttons) and the technical session
      identifier (see "Local browser storage"). They let the agent point at a specific
      place in the CV and assign your messages to one conversation. No other details
      about you and no content from other websites are sent.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Fetching the agent card:</strong> On the pages that display the agent's
      reachability status, its public agent card (<em>agent-card.json</em>) is fetched
      once as the page loads, without any action on your part. Your IP address is
      transmitted to the endpoint named above in doing so and recorded there in the
      computer's operational log (see "Operational logs"). No input is sent and nothing
      is stored in your browser. On every other page, including the legal
      notice and this privacy notice, that fetch does not happen.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Conversation history:</strong> So the agent can build on earlier
      messages, it keeps the history of a conversation in memory. It is lost when the
      service restarts. In addition, the Claude software stores a session file on the
      computer for every answer, containing your message, the conversation so far and
      the answer.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Conversation logs:</strong> Every question and every answer is logged in
      plain text together with the conversation identifier, its sequence number and the
      response time. The logs are kept at <strong>Elastic Cloud</strong> in an account
      of BKS-Lab GmbH, stored in Frankfurt am Main (Amazon Web Services region
      eu-central-1). They can be read by Michael Boiman and by anyone with access to
      that account or to one of its access keys. BKS-Lab GmbH also uses the account for
      other projects, including a client project in which such a key is currently
      stored. The logs serve operation and troubleshooting, detecting abuse and
      improving the answers (see "Evaluations"). This logging has been in place since
      6 August 2026.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Operational logs:</strong> In addition, logs without conversation content
      are kept at Elastic Cloud and on the computer (conversation identifier, time,
      duration, length of request and answer, outcome). The operational log on the
      computer also records every request to the endpoint with your IP address, the
      address requested and the outcome, including the agent card fetch. The
      operational logs serve secure and stable operation and the prevention of abuse.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Consulting other agents:</strong> Questions about BKS-Lab GmbH or the
      open-bridge project are passed on in general form, without your name or contact
      details, to two further agents. They run on the same computer and work the same
      way (answers via Anthropic, logs at Elastic Cloud).
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Inquiries, appointments and notifications</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Meeting requests and inquiries:</strong> If you would like a meeting with
      Michael Boiman or send him an inquiry, for example about a project, a position, a
      cooperation or an offer, the agent records your details: name, contact details,
      company and website (if given), topic, preferred time, your request, your answers
      to its follow-up questions and the last messages of the conversation. Added to
      this are its assessment of the request and, for inquiries, a recommendation and a
      draft reply for Michael Boiman. The details are stored on the computer and
      forwarded to Michael Boiman by email. Michael Boiman decides on your request
      himself. Only sales offers addressed to him are declined by the agent itself,
      following his instructions.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Office hours (if offered):</strong> If the agent offers fixed meeting
      slots, it can book one of them for you. To do so, it sends a confirmation code to
      the email address you provide. The slot is only booked once you enter the code in
      the chat. You and Michael Boiman then receive an email with a calendar
      invitation. The email address, name (if given), topic, slot and booking status
      are stored. To prevent abuse, the number of codes per conversation, per address and
      per hour is limited.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Notifications to Michael Boiman:</strong> The agent sends its emails
      through the mailbox ai@bks-lab.com of BKS-Lab GmbH at
      <strong>Microsoft 365</strong>. Michael Boiman receives them in his mailbox at
      <strong>Google</strong> (Gmail). Once a day he also receives an overview of
      conversations that remained open after the agent's follow-up questions and of
      inquiries without their own email. If enabled, the agent additionally notifies him
      of a meeting request via the <strong>Telegram</strong> messenger, containing only
      the type of request, the preferred time and a short reference, without your
      name, contact details or any text from you. If Michael Boiman responds there, the
      agent sends you his answer (confirmation with calendar invitation, proposal of a
      different time or cancellation) at the email address from your meeting request.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Abuse reports:</strong> If the agent detects an abuse attempt, such as an
      attempt to manipulate it or to obtain non-public information, a threat or spam, or
      clearly targeted research about Michael Boiman, it reports this to Michael Boiman
      by email, with a short description, its assessment of who is asking and the last
      messages of the conversation. It keeps the same details on the computer. You are
      not notified of this in the chat.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Information that needs no further data about you:</strong> The agent
      names free slots from an overview of busy times, without the content of any
      appointment. Its information on project capacity is based on a figure Michael
      Boiman maintains himself. Neither processes any data about you beyond the
      conversation.
    </li>
  </ul>

  <h3>Evaluations</h3>
  <p>
    Once a week, the conversation logs are automatically evaluated for questions the
    agent could not answer, or answered only evasively. Where needed, a language model
    from Anthropic groups the questions and answers found into topics. Only Michael
    Boiman receives the result, with individual example questions, by email. It serves
    to extend the public information in the CV.
  </p>

  <h3>Local browser storage</h3>
  <p>
    With your first message, the chat stores a random technical session identifier in
    your browser's local storage (localStorage), not when the page loads. It is sent
    with every message so a conversation can continue across a page reload, and it
    appears in the logs and inquiries described above. Conversations from the same
    browser can be linked through it. The browser also remembers whether you opened or
    closed the chat window and which size you set. This storage is required for the
    function you use (§ 25(2) no. 2 TDDDG) and is not used for tracking. You remove
    these entries by deleting the site data for mboiman.github.io in your browser. No
    analytics or advertising cookies are set.
  </p>

  <h3>Legal bases</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Answering your questions, conversation history, the agent card fetch,
      conversation and operational logs, consulting other agents, abuse reports,
      limiting confirmation codes and the weekly evaluation: Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. The legitimate interest lies in answering
      questions about Michael Boiman and his work, in secure and stable operation, in
      preventing abuse and in improving the answers.
    </li>
    <li>
      Meeting requests, inquiries, office hours bookings including the confirmation
      code, the notifications to Michael Boiman and his answer to you: Art. 6(1)(b)
      GDPR (steps taken at your request prior to a possible contract). If you inquire
      on behalf of a company, the legal basis is Art. 6(1)(f) GDPR. The legitimate
      interest lies in handling business inquiries.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    No automated decision-making within the meaning of Art. 22 GDPR takes place.
  </p>
  <p class="legal-muted">
    Note: Please do not enter confidential information or special categories of
    personal data (e.g. health, religious or political data) into the chat. For a
    meeting request, a name and one way to reach you are enough.
  </p>

  <h2>4. Recipients and transfers to third countries</h2>
  <p>Within the scope described, the following parties receive data:</p>
  <ul>
    <li><strong>GitHub</strong> (GitHub, Inc., USA): hosting of the website.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Cloudflare</strong> (Cloudflare, Inc., USA): transport and protection of
      the chat.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Anthropic</strong> (Anthropic Ireland, Limited, Ireland): generating the
      answers, including for the questions passed on to the other agents, and grouping
      topics in the weekly evaluation. For this the agent uses a Claude subscription of
      Michael Boiman, not Anthropic's offering for business customers. Anthropic
      therefore processes the data under its own responsibility, according to its terms
      of use and its privacy policy. There is no data processing agreement. Whether
      Anthropic also uses the content to train its models depends on a setting in that
      subscription. The data is also processed in the USA. According to Anthropic, it
      bases transfers there on the EU Standard Contractual Clauses.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>BKS-Lab GmbH</strong>: provides the logging account at Elastic Cloud and
      the sending mailbox at Microsoft 365. <strong>Elastic</strong> (Elasticsearch
      B.V., Netherlands, storage location Frankfurt am Main) and
      <strong>Microsoft</strong> (Microsoft Ireland Operations Limited, Ireland) are
      engaged for this as processors.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Google</strong> (Google Ireland Limited, Ireland): Michael Boiman's
      mailbox, which receives the agent's emails.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Telegram</strong> (if enabled): notification to Michael Boiman about a
      meeting request. The provider is based outside the EU. The message contains no
      details by which Telegram could identify you.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <p>
    GitHub, Cloudflare, Elastic, Microsoft and Google are based in the USA or belong to
    groups of companies based in the USA, so data may also be processed there. For
    these providers, transfers to the USA take place on the basis of the EU-U.S. Data
    Privacy Framework (where the respective company is certified) or the EU Standard
    Contractual Clauses pursuant to Art. 46 GDPR. No data is passed on to any other
    third parties.
  </p>

  <h2>5. Retention period</h2>
  <p>
    Once the following periods have expired, the data is deleted unless statutory
    retention obligations apply.
  </p>
  <ul>
    <li>
      <strong>Conversation history in memory:</strong> transient, until the service
      restarts or it is displaced by newer conversations.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Conversation logs (questions and answers):</strong> 90 days.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Operational logs without conversation content,</strong> including the IP
      addresses in the computer's operational log: 30 days.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Session files of the Claude software:</strong> 30 days.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Meeting requests and inquiries:</strong> 12 months. If an inquiry leads to
      a working relationship, the periods prescribed for that apply.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Abuse reports on the computer:</strong> 90 days.</li>
    <li><strong>Office hours bookings:</strong> 12 months from the appointment.</li>
    <li><strong>Office hours confirmation codes:</strong> 24 hours.</li>
    <li>
      <strong>Emails and Telegram messages to Michael Boiman</strong> (notifications,
      overviews, evaluations, abuse reports), in his mailbox and in the sending mailbox:
      12 months.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>The agent's emails to you</strong> (confirmation code, calendar
      invitation, Michael Boiman's answer) in the sending mailbox: 12 months.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>At Anthropic:</strong> according to Anthropic, 30 days if the use for
      training is switched off in the subscription, otherwise up to five years. Content
      flagged by Anthropic's safety systems up to two years.
    </li>
    <li>
      <strong>Session identifier and window settings in the browser:</strong> until you
      delete the site data.
    </li>
    <li><strong>Server access data from hosting:</strong> as determined by GitHub.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>6. Your rights</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to access (Art. 15), rectification (Art. 16), erasure (Art. 17),
    restriction of processing (Art. 18), data portability (Art. 20) and the right to
    object to processing based on legitimate interests (Art. 21 GDPR). You may withdraw
    any consent given at any time with effect for the future (Art. 7(3) GDPR). An
    informal message to
    <a href="mailto:mboiman@gmail.com">mboiman@gmail.com</a> is sufficient.
  </p>
  <p>
    This includes the chat: you can object to your conversation being logged and
    request that your details be deleted. So Michael Boiman can find your conversation,
    please state the date, the approximate time and, if possible, your first question.
    If you do not want your conversation logged, please write an email instead of using
    the chat.
  </p>

  <h2>7. Right to lodge a complaint</h2>
  <p>
    You have the right to lodge a complaint with a data protection supervisory
    authority, for example the Hessian Commissioner for Data Protection and Freedom of
    Information, Postfach 3163, 65021 Wiesbaden, Germany.
  </p>

  <h2>8. Changes</h2>
  <p>
    This privacy policy will be updated whenever the service or the legal framework
    changes.
  </p>
</LegalLayout>
